          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in Skia, a 2D graphics library used in Chromium. A remote attacker could exploit an uninitialized resource vulnerability by tricking a user into opening a specially crafted HTML page. This could potentially allow the attacker to read sensitive memory within the browser's sandbox, leading to information disclosure.",
