        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in ANGLE, a component used in Google Chrome. A remote attacker could exploit an out-of-bounds write vulnerability by tricking a user into visiting a specially crafted HTML page. This could potentially allow the attacker to execute arbitrary code outside of the browser's security sandbox, leading to a compromise of the affected system.",
