            "text": "A flaw was found in ANGLE, a component used in Google Chrome on Android. This buffer overflow vulnerability allows a remote attacker to execute arbitrary code outside of the browser's security sandbox. The exploitation occurs when a user visits a specially crafted HTML page, leading to a severe compromise of the affected system.",
